WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.295
Sovereign AI means deliberate control over data, models, infrastructure, access, policy, and operations.

2
00:00:07.295 --> 00:00:18.792
It begins with data classification: know what prompts, documents, embeddings, outputs, logs, and evaluation records may contain before routing them into an AI workflow.

3
00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:24.897
Data sensitivity should guide deployment, retention, access, and monitoring decisions.

4
00:00:24.897 --> 00:00:30.606
Choose local, private, cloud, or hybrid deployment based on the work, not on slogans.

5
00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:37.584
Consider sensitivity, performance, cost, usability, operational capacity, and vendor commitments.

6
00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:43.055
Treat private RAG as a permissioned knowledge system, not just a vector database.

7
00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:49.636
Preserve source provenance, permissions, freshness, tenant boundaries, and lifecycle status.

8
00:00:49.636 --> 00:00:52.253
Scope model and tool access carefully.

9
00:00:52.253 --> 00:01:02.878
A model endpoint, retrieval collection, tool, agent workflow, or administrative function should have clear permissions and audit-ready policy decisions.

10
00:01:02.878 --> 00:01:07.476
Monitor quality and usage without over-collecting sensitive logs.

11
00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:12.868
Evaluation, observability, and privacy controls should reinforce each other.

12
00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:18.894
Finally, plan for infrastructure cost, reliability, backup, recovery, and governance.

13
00:01:18.894 --> 00:01:25.634
Define owners for models, vendors, retrieval collections, policy, incidents, and change control.

14
00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:33.801
A sovereign AI program succeeds when control is practical, visible, and maintainable across everyday engineering work.

15
00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.814
The durable habit is to make control visible.

16
00:01:36.814 --> 00:01:48.549
Teams should be able to point to the data rule, the deployment choice, the approved model, the retrieval boundary, the tool permission, the monitoring decision, and the owner.

17
00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:57.747
When those decisions are documented and reviewable, sovereign AI becomes a repeatable operating model instead of a one-off experiment.
